    "annotations": {
      "notes": [
        "The caller's BYE carries a one-rung ladder (RFC 3261 §17.1.2.2 Timer E, T1 = 500 ms) and the callee answers the teardown it takes at once. A ladder paces ONE leg's transaction and gates nothing else, so the teardown is answered long before the rung: a run whose rung precedes the answer has parked itself inside a timer that was never a barrier."
      ]
    },
    "family": "transparent",
    "id": "ladder-beside-the-loop",
    "lanes": {
      "upstream-fake": "ok"
    },
    "origin": "authored",
